# Local secrets for Wrangler. Copy this file to .dev.vars only when a value below is real.
# .dev.vars is the local secret file. When it exists, Wrangler uses it and does not read .env.
# Leave every line commented until the value exists. Commented lines do not override wrangler.jsonc.
# Do not invent values, and do not copy a production key into this file.
# Never commit .dev.vars, .env, or .secrets/.

# Not used on the public website
# SITE_ACCESS and CMS_SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL are already set in wrangler.jsonc.
# DB and BUCKET are bindings in that file, not secrets.

# Cloudflare Access — required before staff sign-in can succeed
# Set these only after the account owner creates an Access application.
# Localhost cannot complete the browser sign-in even after these are set.
# ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN="https://team-name.cloudflareaccess.com"
# ACCESS_AUD="access-application-audience"

# Google Sheets test copy — optional, and off until both values are set
# Use a separate test spreadsheet. Do not use the production workbook or its Apps Script.
# Generate a new key with: node scripts/create-intake-keys.mjs
# Put only the new public key in the test Apps Script.
# SHEETS_WEBHOOK_URL="https://script.google.com/macros/s/TEST-DEPLOYMENT-ID/exec"
# INTAKE_SIGNING_KEY='{"kty":"RSA","n":"REPLACE","e":"AQAB","d":"REPLACE"}'

# One-time brochure import — optional. The route still requires this secret or a Super Admin.
# CMS_BROCHURE_IMPORT_TOKEN="replace-with-a-random-secret"
